{"base_rate":0.5421487603305785,"brier":0.217781652892562,"bss":0.12263879655718934,"bss_hi":0.21001430573895155,"bss_lo":0.03801151764688287,"chart":{"base":[530.7,212.7],"fp":[384.5,251.7],"lead":"62,262.7 272,262 482,261.2 692,260.9","note":{"base":"skill 0.12 — higher than 19% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +12pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 68% of cities","rel":"promised 13% → rained 21%; promised 96% → rained 73%"},"rel":"142.7,375.1 309.2,275.5 445.2,235.8 571.2,125.5 668.9,152.5"},"country":"VI","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09416528925619833,"ess":447.56835596200136,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Charlotte Amalie</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Charlotte Amalie rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 3 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(7%), there is still roughly a <b>18%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 605 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-04-20. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nCHARLOTTE AMALIE 1.2 NNW, 2.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.12, ranked 175 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(148&ndash;187) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>54</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>55%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>66%</td><td class='num'><b>60%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>77%</td><td class='num'><b>72%</b></td><td class='num'>58</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>60</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>64%</b></td><td class='num'>59</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">3 of 10 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Charlotte Amalie</b> <span class=\"muted\">U.S. Virgin Islands</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;54% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 54% of days.</p><p>The forecast did only slightly better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">3 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<detai